# Kaziro — Svelte Frontend Rules

# ================================

# Applies to: frontend/src/**/\*.svelte, frontend/src/**/\*.ts

## Framework & Syntax

- Use Svelte 5 with runes. Never use Svelte 4 reactive statements (`$:`) or stores (`writable()`).
- Rune usage:
  - `$state()` for local mutable state
  - `$derived()` for computed values (replaces `$: derived = ...`)
  - `$effect()` for side effects (replaces `onMount` for data-driven effects)
  - `$props()` for component props
- All component scripts use `<script lang="ts">`.
- All event handlers use the new Svelte 5 syntax: `onclick={handler}` not `on:click={handler}`.

## File & Folder Structure

```
frontend/src/
├── routes/                    # SvelteKit pages
│   ├── +layout.svelte         # Root layout (auth guard, nav)
│   ├── +layout.server.ts      # Root load (appearance cookie → theme)
│   ├── onboarding/
│   ├── dashboard/
│   ├── jobs/
│   │   ├── +page.svelte       # Job list
│   │   └── [id]/
│   │       ├── +page.svelte   # Job detail
│   │       └── apply/
│   ├── applications/
│   └── settings/
├── lib/
│   ├── components/            # Reusable UI components (PascalCase)
│   │   ├── jobs/              # Job-specific components
│   │   ├── applications/      # Application-specific
│   │   └── ui/                # Generic UI (Button, Badge, Modal)
│   ├── api/                   # API client functions
│   │   ├── client.ts          # Base fetch wrapper with auth headers
│   │   ├── jobs.ts
│   │   ├── applications.ts
│   │   └── profile.ts
│   ├── stores/                # Svelte 5 rune-based state (auth, notifications)
│   ├── types/                 # TypeScript interfaces matching API schemas
│   └── utils/                 # Pure utility functions
```

## Component Rules

- One component per file. File name = component name (PascalCase).
- Props must be typed with a TypeScript interface: `const { job }: { job: JobPosting } = $props()`.
- Components must not make API calls directly — receive data via props or use TanStack Query.
- Extract any logic block > 10 lines into a utility function in `lib/utils/`.
- Never use `document.querySelector` or direct DOM manipulation — use Svelte bindings.
- All async operations in components must handle loading and error states explicitly.

## API Layer (lib/api/)

- All API calls go through `lib/api/client.ts` which:
  - Attaches the Supabase auth token to every request
  - Handles 401 responses by redirecting to login
  - Throws typed errors with `code` and `message`
- Each resource has its own file (`jobs.ts`, `applications.ts`, etc.).
- API functions are plain async functions, not classes.
- Use TanStack Query (`@tanstack/svelte-query`) for all data fetching in components.
- Mutations use `createMutation()` with proper `onSuccess` / `onError` handlers.

## TypeScript Types (lib/types/)

- Every API response shape has a corresponding TypeScript interface in `lib/types/`.
- Types mirror the Pydantic response schemas from the backend.
- Use `type` for simple shapes, `interface` for extensible objects.
- Never use `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow it properly.
- Shared enums (e.g., `Classification`, `ApplicationStatus`) are defined once in `lib/types/enums.ts`.

## Styling Rules

- TailwindCSS utility classes only. No `<style>` blocks in components unless unavoidable.
- Use DaisyUI component classes for form elements, modals, and alerts.
- Use semantic color names from the Kaziro theme (defined in `tailwind.config.ts`):
  - `primary` — main brand colour
  - `secondary` — accent
  - `success` — good fit / confirmed actions
  - `warning` — maybe / pending states
  - `error` — rejected / error states
- Classification badges: `GOOD_FIT` → `badge-success`, `MAYBE` → `badge-warning`, `REJECT` → `badge-error`.
- Never use arbitrary Tailwind values (`w-[347px]`) — use spacing scale.

## Real-time (WebSocket)

- WebSocket connection is managed in `lib/stores/notifications.ts`.
- Components subscribe to notification events via the store — never open their own WebSocket.
- Always disconnect WebSocket on component destroy (`$effect` cleanup).
- Show a toast notification for: `evaluation_complete`, `documents_ready`.

## Forms

- Use native `<form>` with SvelteKit `use:enhance` for progressive enhancement.
- Validate on the client with Zod schemas that mirror the backend Pydantic schemas.
- Show field-level errors next to each input, not just a global error message.
- Disable submit buttons while mutation is in progress.
- Never use `form.reset()` after a successful mutation — use TanStack Query invalidation.

## Performance

- Use `+page.ts` load functions for initial data — avoid client-side-only data fetching for page content.
- Lazy-load heavy components (PDF viewer, rich text editor) with dynamic `import()`.
- Paginated lists must use virtual scrolling if items exceed 100.
- Images must always include `width`, `height`, and `alt` attributes.

## Accessibility

- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Use semantic HTML: `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation.
- All form inputs must have associated `<label>` elements.
- Use `aria-live="polite"` on areas that update with pipeline status.
